CSC Newsletter

CSC together with University of Helsinki and Aalto University is training two teams for the international Student Cluster Competetion (SCC) organized by the HPC-AI Advisory Council as a part of the ISC25 conference. Previously, three different CSC led student teams have participated SCC within the Supercomputing conference (SC22, SC23, and SC24). This is the first time Finnish team is participating SCC within the ISC, and the first time there are two Finnish teams competing.

Both teams were selected to the virtual competition that takes place in April and uses computing resources from Deutsches Klimarechenzentrum (DKRZ) and Pittsburgh Supercomputing Center (PSC). Additionally, the CSC/UoH team will compete against 9 university teams from South Africa, Switzerland, Germany, Singapore, Taiwan, USA, China, Spain and United Kingdom in the on-site event at the ISC25 conference in Hamburg in June 10-12. In the on-site competition the teams work on their own mini-clusters, which for the CSC/UoH Team Lumikko will be provided by Eviden who is the vendor for CSC's Puhti and Mahti and the coming Roihu supercomputer. 

In both competitions the six person student teams face various HPC related challenges like running benchmarks, reproducing results from scientific articles and trying to compile and run previously unknown HPC applications. CSC's goal in training and supporting the teams is to give the students an intensive and practical introduction to HPC, cluster management and working in an supercomputing environment and have lots of fun while learning. We hope that students have unforgettable experience in participating an international competition as a team, and that the competition boosts their studies and future careers.
